  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-23T10:29:49.503Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Just like how people bring a laptop to Starbucks or have LAN parties or internet cafes, what if you could bring your computer into VRChat? Either a placeable prop or a feature that can be added to maps. Both a motioncontroller interface and a way to use mouse and keyboard without messing up your hand positions, e.g. lock hands in place on the virtual laptop or something.\n\nFor both performance and privacy reasons this would be client-side only, everyone else can see some placeholder image.\n\nA more advanced version could have some limited sharing ability. So you could share a screenshot or youtube video or clip or whatever things are deemed safe. Maybe some way to use Twitch or something to stream to a big screen in the room for everyone to see? Would be cool for tournament-style stuff.\n\nMy personal use-case is to access my tabletop RPG resources without going into the steam overlay or taking the headset off. Also having everyone able to access Roll20 in-game would remove the headaches of trying to find a map with the right dice and pen props.",
